title: '[pgas-allowance] Benchmark the account kill and re-creation on the PGAS fee path'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The `charge_pgas` benchmark funded the caller with `u64::MAX` PGAS, so the fee withdrawal
    never dropped the caller below the asset's minimum balance and the benchmark never measured
    the worst case branch. The extension withdraws with `Precision::Exact` and
    `Preservation::Expendable`, which removes the `Assets::Account` entry.

    The benchmark now funds the caller with exactly the fee, so the kill and the re-creation both
    happen inside the measured block, and asserts the resulting balance. Runtimes using `ChargePGAS` must regenerate
    `pallet_pgas_allowance` weights.

crates:
- name: pallet-pgas-allowance
  bump: patch
